    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n32023" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐκθηλ-ύνω</span></b> , aor.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-εθήλυνα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.H.
					7.9
				</span></i>
			 :—<i>soften, weaken,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ σκέλος ἐκτεθηλυσμένον γίνεται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hp.
					<u>Art.</u>
					52
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				56
			</span></i>; <i>make effeminate,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στρατιὰν ταῖς ἡδοναῖς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Str.
					5.4.13
				</span></i>
			 ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὴν νεότητα ταῖς
			ἀγωγαῖς</span> D.H.l.c.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ψυχάς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Corn.
					<u>ND</u>
					20
				</span></i>
			 :—
				Pass.
			, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐκτεθηλυμμένος καὶ τῇ ψυχῇ καὶ τῷ
					σώματι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plb.
					36.15.2
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				28.21.3
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.C.
				50.27
			</span></i> ; of plants, <i>become enfeebled,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>CP</u>
				3.1.3
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> Gramm.,
				<i>make a feminine of,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				EM
				473.35
			</span></i>.</div>
